        "orario": "07:51",
        "timestamp": 1776059508,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Fidesz MEP László attributes loss to low turnout of 'undecided voters' and EU 'economic stagnation' Europe Issued on: 13/04/2026 - 07:51 Modified: 13/04/2026 - 08:04 FRANCE 24's Senior European Editor Armen Georgian is pleased to welcome András László, MEP for Patriots for Europe / Fidesz. According to Laszio, the outcome cannot be reduced to a single campaign misstep or policy failure. He says governing parties across Europe are all under pressure from economic stagnation. But he does accuse the opposition of a \"filthy and hate-filled campaign\" that prioritised personalities over substance and concrete policy positions. He warns the newly empowered majority holds significant institutional authority, yet its policy direction remains largely undefined. Hungary's 'return to Europe: Peaceful revolution' embraces new path away from Russia and autocracy 13/04/2026 Europe Trump's incendiary rhetoric fuels 'chaos and confusion', driving NATO allies toward self-reliance 12/04/2026 Europe 'Undeterred’: Hungarian investigative journalist faces threats and espionage accusations from Orbán 12/04/2026 Europe Orban and Magyar face off in historic vote 12/04/2026 Europe Orban's 16-year grip on power under threat from Magyar 12/04/2026 Europe Hungary: Centre-right Tisza party tipped to defeat Orban's Fidesz 12/04/2026 Europe Polls open in Hungary crunch vote 12/04/2026 Europe Hungary: Orban and Magyar on the home stretch 12/04/2026 Europe Among Magyar's supporters, \"one word keeps coming up: hope\" 12/04/2026 Europe"
